  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * @ingroup groupFilters
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * @defgroup FIR_decimate Finite Impulse Response (FIR) Decimator
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * These functions combine an FIR filter together with a decimator.
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * They are used in multirate systems for reducing the sample rate of a signal without introducing 
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Conceptually, the functions are equivalent to the block diagram below:
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \image html FIRDecimator.gif "Components included in the FIR Decimator functions"
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * When decimating by a factor of <code>M</code>, the signal should be prefiltered by a lowpass fil
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * cutoff frequency of <code>1/M</code> in order to prevent aliasing distortion.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The user of the function is responsible for providing the filter coefficients.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The FIR decimator functions provided in the CMSIS DSP Library combine the FIR filter and the dec
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Instead of calculating all of the FIR filter outputs and discarding <code>M-1</code> out of ever
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * samples output by the decimator are computed.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on blocks of input and output data.
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrc</code> points to an array of <code>blockSize</code> input values and
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <code>pDst</code> points to an array of <code>blockSize/M</code> output values.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * In order to have an integer number of output samples <code>blockSize</code>
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * must always be a multiple of the decimation factor <code>M</code>.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The library provides separate functions for Q15, Q31 and floating-point data types.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm:
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The FIR portion of the algorithm uses the standard form filter:
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *    y[n] = b[0] * x[n] + b[1] * x[n-1] + b[2] * x[n-2] + ...+ b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps+1]
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * where, <code>b[n]</code> are the filter coefficients.
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The <code>pCoeffs</code> points to a coefficient array of size <code>numTaps</code>.
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Coefficients are stored in time reversed order.
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *    {b[numTaps-1], b[numTaps-2], b[N-2], ..., b[1], b[0]}
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> points to a state array of size <code>numTaps + blockSize - 1</code>.
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Samples in the state buffer are stored in the order:
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *    {x[n-numTaps+1], x[n-numTaps], x[n-numTaps-1], x[n-numTaps-2]....x[0], x[1], ..., x[blockSize
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed, the coefficients are unto
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data struct
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable array should be al
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par Initialization Functions
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\cc1rKCV9.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * - Checks to make sure that the size of the input is a multiple of the decimation factor.
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instan
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * numTaps, pCoeffs, M (decimation factor), pState. Also set all of the values in pState to zero.
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * The code below statically initializes each of the 3 different data type filter instance structur
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_decimate_instance_f32 S = {M, numTaps, pCoeffs, pState};
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_decimate_instance_q31 S = {M, numTaps, pCoeffs, pState};
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *arm_fir_decimate_instance_q15 S = {M, numTaps, pCoeffs, pState};
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * where <code>M</code> is the decimation factor; <code>numTaps</code> is the number of filter coef
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer;
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> is the address of the state buffer.
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Be sure to set the values in the state buffer to zeros when doing static initialization.
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  *
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the fixed-point versions of the FIR decimate filter functions.
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * In particular, the overflow and saturation behavior of the accumulator used in each function mus
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  * Refer to the function specific documentation below for usage guidelines.
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_decimate_f32.c ****  */
